This app uses the following third-party component to encrypt the keyboard's
own database (agentic_keyboard_database) on the device (KEYBOARD-048).

1. SQLCipher for Android (Community Edition)
   Artifact: net.zetetic:sqlcipher-android:4.20.0
   License: BSD-3-Clause (BSD-style), Copyright (c) 2008-2023, ZETETIC LLC
   https://github.com/sqlcipher/sqlcipher-android
   https://www.zetetic.net/sqlcipher/license/
   The full licence text ships in the APK as assets/third_party/SQLCipher-LICENSE.txt.
   The native library bundles SQLite (public domain) and LibTomCrypt (public
   domain / Unlicense) as its crypto provider; no OpenSSL, no GPL code.
   Declared dependencies: kotlin-stdlib (Apache-2.0), androidx.sqlite (Apache-2.0).
